sizu-writer Repository Version History
======================================

v1.0.0 (Release Date: 2026-08-04)
---------------------------------
- Initial release. A Flask application that turns a short memo into a
  post body and title candidates for Shizuka na Internet, with the
  generation core (sizu_writer/) kept independent from the web layer so
  that cli.py can settle the prompts before any screen is involved.
- The prompts live in prompts/*.md, outside the Python package, so that
  adjusting the writing policy needs neither a code change nor a
  reinstall.
- The server keeps no state: the memo and the current body travel with
  the form, which is what lets the titles be regenerated without a
  session store.
- The repository is written in English throughout, including the
  screens, the documents and the prompts. Only the generated post is
  Japanese, because the medium is. The Japanese that remains in the
  source is load bearing: the phrases formatter.py matches against a
  generated body, the fixtures that exercise it, and the openings and
  closings quoted in the prompts and the specifications as the literal
  strings the model must not produce. The screens are marked lang="en",
  with lang="ja" on the elements carrying the memo and the draft.
- Documented to the level of id774/ai-digest: a README covering the
  concept, installation, every setting, both entry points, the notices,
  the failures and the deployment, plus doc/PROMPTS.md for the prompt
  layer, which is where the quality of the output actually lives.
- OPENAI_TEMPERATURE is validated like every other numeric setting, so
  a bad value is refused by name instead of raising a bare float error.
- Not implemented yet, and deliberately left for a later change: the
  space inserted between full width characters and ASCII, the
  json_schema and none response format modes, the Origin check on POST,
  and LOG_PAYLOAD. PROMPT_RELOAD is absent for a different reason: it
  was to switch off a cache, and no cache was built, so the prompts are
  read on every generation already.
- Return a safe HTTP 413 response when a submitted request exceeds the
  server limit, without parsing the oversized form again.
